<div class="hero"><div class="kicker">document compiler · not a CMS</div>
<h1>dog<span class="em">bed</span><br>the dog builds its own docs</h1>
<p class="sub">A Knap template plus a JSON object goes in, a finished HTML document comes out. One static binary — no runtime, no JavaScript, no database, no edit button.</p>
<div class="cta"><a class="primary" href="cli.html">the CLI</a><a class="ghost" href="https://github.com/drawmeanelephant/dogbed">github</a></div>
<img src="assets/oliver-dogbed.webp" alt="oliver the Weimaraner in an orange HTML5 cape, asleep on a dog bed"></div>

{{ pipeline | code_block }}

<div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3><span class="ic">01</span> two halves</h3><p>k4o templates, oliver renders — dogbed joins data and document in one binary.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3><span class="ic">02</span> knap-faithful</h3><p>The knap-0.6.0 engine: loops, conditions, filters, typed values — spec first.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3><span class="ic">03</span> pipe-friendly</h3><p>stdin in, stdout out, exit codes like a compiler. Errors never half-emit.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3><span class="ic">04</span> extensions</h3><p>Highlights, math, callouts, task lists, footnotes — Oliver 1.3 parses them natively.</p></div></div>

